+The clinic publishes the veterinarians it employs with the specialties each holds, listed a page at a time. A veterinarian holding no specialty is shown as having none rather than left blank `[REQ-VET-001]`. The same directory is also published in a machine-readable form; this second surface is a supported capability, not an artifact `[REQ-VET-003]`.
+
+The directory can be requested narrowed to a single specialty, on both surfaces `[REQ-VET-003]`. The reader asks for one specialty by name, and only the veterinarians holding it are returned; on the page the result is still listed a page at a time. Matching is on the whole specialty name and disregards letter case — it is not a prefix match. A specialty that no veterinarian holds returns an empty directory in the normal structure, not an error. An empty or whitespace-only specialty is treated as no filter at all, the same way an empty owner search returns every owner. When no specialty is asked for, both surfaces behave exactly as before `[REQ-VET-003]`. The filter is available by request only: this requirement adds no on-screen control — no form, dropdown, or link — for choosing a specialty, and a visible control may follow as a separate request. Navigation between pages preserves an active specialty, so a filtered directory stays navigable `[REQ-VET-003]`.
 
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given the clinic's veterinarians, when the directory is opened, then each name and its specialties are listed a page at a time.
 - `[REQ-VET-001]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian is shown as having none.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the machine-readable veterinarian list, when it is requested with no specialty, then it returns the full directory as a supported surface.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty that one or more veterinarians hold, when the directory page or the machine-readable list is requested for it, then only those veterinarians are returned, and the page still lists them a page at a time.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty name differing from a held specialty only by letter case, when either surface is requested for it, then it matches; given only the start of a specialty name, then it does not match.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty that no veterinarian holds, when either surface is requested for it, then an empty directory is returned in the normal structure, not an error.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given an empty or whitespace-only specialty, when either surface is requested with it, then it is treated as no filter and the full directory is returned.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given no specialty at all, when either surface is requested, then it behaves exactly as before this requirement.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a filtered directory page with further pages, when a page-navigation link is followed, then the next page carries the same specialty and stays filtered.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. A veterinarian's specialties are presented in a stable order rather than an arbitrary one.
